.TH "FSV" 1 "2026-10-20" "3.0" "SlackBuilds.org"
.SH NAME
fsv \- 3D filesystem visualizer
.\" RST source for fsv(1) man page. Convert with:
.
.\" rst2man.py fsv.rst > fsv.1
.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.sp
fsv [\fIrootdir\fP] [\fI\-options\fP]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.sp
\fBfsv\fP (pronounced eff\-ess\-vee) is a file system visualizer in cyberspace. It
lays out files and directories in three dimensions, geometrically
representing the file system hierarchy to allow visual overview and
analysis. \fBfsv\fP can visualize a modest home directory, a workstation\(aqs
hard drive, or any arbitrarily large collection of files, limited only
by the host computer\(aqs memory and graphics hardware.
.sp
\fBfsv\fP is a clone of SGI\(aqs \fBfsn\fP, which was featured in the movie Jurassic Park.
.sp
Full documentation is available via the Help \-> Contents menu option, or
in /usr/doc/fsv\-3.0/html/fsv.html
.SH OPTIONS
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \fBrootdir\fP
Root directory for visualization (defaults to current directory)
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B  \-\-mapv
Start in MapV mode (default)
.TP
.B  \-\-treev
Start in TreeV mode
.TP
.B  \-\-help
Print built\-in help and exit
.UNINDENT
.SH AUTHORS
.sp
